    "guidance": "Use for represented intermediate entries or red-versus-blue phase ambiguity only when the caller can infer the semantic phase from current geometry. It passed 9/12 in-distribution runs. Require drawer_position >0.26 m and select: drawer_release_to_red before red contact; red_grasp_transport_place while closing/carrying/descending red; red_release_to_blue after supported release and during transit; blue_pickup for blue approach/closure/lift. Avoid guessing the phase, and do not assume this local-TCP representation handles large red/goal displacement. Wrong phase can select the wrong object or gripper behavior. Watch for phase/geometry disagreement, closure on the wrong object, absent red co-motion, red off-pad/following retreat, blue not under TCP at closure, unreachable IK targets, and especially loss of drawer opening. All three validation failures ended with drawer_position <=0.26; two also had red off-pad, while one transiently met the exit rule and ended with red on-pad but the drawer nearly closed (0.0521 m). Handoff: after supported red release use red_release_to_blue, then blue_pickup; switch cleanly to blue_insert after red is contained and stationary, drawer_position remains >0.26, and blue/TCP initial-lift co-motion is observed. If phase cannot be determined, prefer h02 rather than guessing."
